bjects from each other.\r\nTags each have a unique identifier, a name, and a color.","title":"TagCreateDto"},"TagDtoAstroResult":{"type":"object","properties":{"error":{"oneOf":[{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/AstroError"},{"type":"null"}],"description":"If the API call failed, this will contain information about the error that occurred."},"success":{"type":"boolean","description":"True if the API call succeeded; false otherwise."},"hasError":{"type":"boolean","description":"True if the API call failed."},"statusCode":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/HttpStatusCode","description":"The HTTP code of the response."},"data":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/TagDto","description":"A Tag is a named categorization you can use to distinguish objects from each other.\r\nTags each have a unique identifier, a name, and a color."}},"description":"An API result that contains different values depending on whether the API call succeeded or failed.\r\nIf the API call succeeded, the `Success` value will be true and you can use the `Data` element.\r\nIf the API call failed, `Success` will be false and the `Error` value will be non-null.","title":"TagDtoAstroResult"},"TagUpdateDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The name of this Tag. When omitted or null, the name is left unchanged."},"color":{"type":["string","null"],"description":"The color that will be used to represent this Tag visually.  This color\r\nis automatically chosen by the application when a user creates a Tag.\r\n            \r\nYou can choose specify any color that can be represented using HTML RGB\r\nsyntax such as `#0088FF`, in the format `RRGGBB`.  You may not use names\r\nfor colors.\r\nWhen omitted or null, the color is left unchanged."}},"description":"A Tag is a named categorization you can use to distinguish objects from each other.\r\nTags each have a unique identifier, a name, and a color.","title":"TagUpdateDto"},"TaskAssigneeDto":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"t